kosha surface

  -- the interface between two regions — the place where contact happens.
  -- every collision involves a surface (or two surfaces meeting).
  -- surfaces are characterised by:
  --   orientation: horizontal (floor, ground), vertical (wall), inclined (ramp, slope)
  --   material: determines coefficient of restitution and friction coefficient
  --   roughness: smooth surface → low friction. rough → high friction.
  --
  -- the surface is the mediator of all contact forces:
  --   normal force: perpendicular to surface. prevents penetration.
  --   friction force: parallel to surface. opposes relative motion.
  --
  -- in chemistry: surface area matters — reactions happen at surfaces.
  -- finely divided materials have huge surface area → react faster.
  -- iron powder burns; iron block does not (same mass, different surface area).

